Z||000000||RICK REIGSTAD||05-15-99||06:12 PM||||THEOGRE THIS ONES FOR YOU! WHEN MY 88GT IDLES WITH THE DEFROSTER ON MY IDLE GO'S FROM 800 RPMS TO 1050-1100 AND BACK TO 800 AND BACK TO 1050-1100 AND SO FORTH IT CYCLES IN FOUR OR FIVE SECOND INTERVALS. EACH TIME THERE IS A CLICK THAT SOUNDS LIKE IT MAY BE THE AIR CONDITIONER CLUTCH. AT LEAST IT SOUNDS LIKE IT MY COME FROM THERE. IF I TURN OFF THE DEFROSTER THEN THE CAR WILL IDLE AT A  CONSTANT 800 RPMS. WHAR GIVES?
Z||000001||Carrolles||05-17-99||10:43 PM||||Does the A/C work?  Does it blow cold air?  It sounds like the compressor is short cycling.  Could be low on freon.<br>Does it idle correctly all the time when the A/C (or defroster) is off?<br>Have you checked the EGR tube for cracks?  A cracked egr tube will cause the idle to hunt.
Z||000002||RICK REIGSTAD||05-18-99||09:00 PM||||Carrolles: the EGR tube is not cracked. However, the freon is low. I did think about the air unit but because it would do it when the defroster and heat was on, made me think of other things. Thanks for the response
Z||000003||Carrolles||05-19-99||06:48 AM||||When the defroster is on, even if the heat is turned up all the way, the A/C compressor cycles on and off to dehumidify the incoming air.<br>Hope this helps,<br>Carroll
Z||000004||theogre||05-19-99||07:50 AM||||pretty near all cars do that now..... at least on my caravan I can unplug the one switch to shut ot iff in the winter. saves a bunch of gas on that hog to have it off.
